## Recording what happens

Use `psql -d {{ db_name }} -c "..."`. In SQL text, write a single quote as two (`''`). After each change, confirm it back in one short line.

- **Find it first**: `SELECT id, {{ primary_field }}, {{ secondary_field }}, current_stage FROM {{ t }} WHERE {{ primary_field }} ILIKE '%name%';` If more than one row matches, ask which.
- **New {{ entity_singular }}**: `INSERT INTO {{ t }} ({{ primary_field }}, {{ secondary_field }}, source_type, date_first_contact, current_stage{% if has_value %}, {{ value_field_prefix }}_text{% endif %}, location, source_link) VALUES (...);` `source_type` must be one of: {{ source_type_options | map('tojson') | join(', ') }}. Leave unknown fields NULL; don't guess them.
- **Stage change**: `UPDATE {{ t }} SET current_stage = '...' WHERE id = ...;` A trigger records the history; never write to `stage_history` yourself.{% if queued_stage %} When a `{{ queued_stage }}` one moves to `{{ baseline_stage }}`, also set `date_first_contact = COALESCE(date_first_contact, CURRENT_DATE)`.{% endif +%}
- **Next step**: `UPDATE {{ t }} SET next_step = '...', next_step_date = 'YYYY-MM-DD' WHERE id = ...;` Turn "Thursday" into a real date and say which date you used. Set both to NULL once it's done.
- **Notes** (debriefs, follow-ups, anything worth keeping): `INSERT INTO {{ entity_singular }}_notes ({{ entity_singular }}_id, note, stage_at_time) SELECT id, '...', current_stage FROM {{ t }} WHERE id = ...;` Keep their words.
{% if has_value %}
- **{{ value_label }}**: put what they were told, as said, in `{{ value_field_prefix }}_text`; fill `{{ value_field_prefix }}_min`/`_max` only with numbers actually stated.
{% endif %}
{% if has_contact %}
- **{{ contact_singular | capitalize }}s**: one row per person in `{{ contact_plural }}` (`name`, `{{ contact_org_field }}`); link it with `{{ t }}.{{ contact_singular }}_id`.
{% endif %}

